        "fact-1": {
          "type": "fact",
          "settings": {
            "tag": "The numbers",
            "title": "Who still smokes, and who now vapes",
            "body": "Roughly one Australian adult in ten smokes every day, and most say they would rather not. Vaping has risen fastest among people under 30, many of whom never touched a cigarette. Both deliver the same drug, so the treatment is the same: a measured dose, a gradual taper and a plan for the hard days.",
