            "link_url": "",
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/home-2.png",
            "image_alt": "Clinician in a bright clinical setting"
          }
        },
        "fact-2": {
          "type": "fact",
          "settings": {
            "tag": "The odds",
            "title": "Why willpower alone has poor odds",
            "body": "Unassisted quit attempts succeed a small fraction of the time. Combining behavioural support with nicotine replacement therapy roughly doubles the chance of stopping for good — which is why every Quity plan pairs medication with a scheduled check-in rather than sending you off with a box.",
            "link_label": "Read the detail",
            "link_url": "",
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/home-4.png",
            "image_alt": "Medication in a practitioner’s hands"
          }
        },
        "fact-3": {
          "type": "fact",
          "settings": {
            "tag": "The timeline",
            "title": "The first fortnight is the hardest",
            "body": "Cravings peak between days three and ten, then fall sharply. Knowing that in advance is half the battle; having the right dose on hand for the peak is the other half. Your doctor reviews the plan at week two and again at week four.",
            "link_label": "Read the detail",
            "link_url": "",
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/home-3.png",
            "image_alt": "Doctor on the phone"
          }
        }
